  "jd_text": "ServiceNow\r\n· 3 hours ago\r\nAssociate Software Engineer, Core Infrastructure - Moveworks\r\nposition\r\nMountain View, CA\r\ntime\r\nFull-time\r\nremote\r\nOnsite\r\nseniority\r\nNew Grad, Entry Level\r\n61%\r\nFAIR MATCH\r\n100%\r\nExp. Level\r\n46%\r\nSkill\r\n67%\r\nIndustry Exp.\r\nServiceNow is a global market leader in innovative AI-enhanced technology, providing solutions to over 8,100 customers, including 85% of the Fortune 500. The Associate Software Engineer will work closely with various teams to understand infrastructure needs, influence the infrastructure roadmap, and execute projects related to core infrastructure and performance improvements of Moveworks systems.\r\nSaaS\r\nArtificial Intelligence (AI)\r\nEnterprise Software\r\nCloud Computing\r\nAgentic AI\r\nBusiness Process Automation (BPA)\r\nCloud Management\r\nRobotic Process Automation (RPA)\r\ncheck\r\nGrowth Opportunities\r\ncheck\r\nH1B Sponsor Likelynote\r\n\r\nInsider Connection @ServiceNow\r\nturboUnlimited\r\nDiscover valuable connections within the company who might provide insights and potential referrals.\r\nGet 3x more responses when you reach out via email instead of LinkedIn.\r\nBeyond your network\r\nY\r\nA\r\nN\r\nP\r\nA\r\nYogesh Kharwandikar & 4 connections\r\nFrom your previous company\r\nfrom your School\r\nC\r\nY\r\nK\r\nM\r\nK\r\nChristopher Zhou & 4 connections\r\n@University of Maryland and...\r\nFind Any Email\r\n\r\nResponsibilities\r\nClosely work with machine learning, search, product, data, and frontend teams, understand their infrastructure needs, influence infrastructure roadmap, and lead as well as execute on various projects\r\nArchitect and build out the core infrastructure and foundational functionalities such as distributed key value store, schema-less data store, authentication and authorization, event streaming, distributed configuration management and hot reloading, rate limiting and circuit breaking, system for feature flags and A/B testing, traffic capture and replay, etc\r\nImprove observability and reliability of Moveworks systems by building and enhancing distributed logging, tracing, monitoring, and alerting infrastructure\r\nDefine methodologies and metrics to measure performance of microservices and product functionalities, identify and fix bottlenecks, as well as improve overall performance and scalability of Moveworks applications\r\nRegularly deliver deadline sensitive work that is interdependent with other engineering teams\r\n\r\nQualification\r\ncheck\r\nRepresents the skills you have\r\nFind out how your skills align with this job's requirements. If anything seems off, you can easily click on the tags to select or unselect skills to reflect your actual expertise.\r\n\r\nBackend distributed systems\r\nPython\r\ncheckGolang\r\nJava\r\ncheckC++\r\ncheckContainers\r\ncheckDocker\r\ncheckCloud infrastructure\r\ncheckAWS\r\nGCP\r\ncheckAzure\r\nOpen source technologies\r\nKafka\r\nElasticsearch\r\nOpensearch\r\nIstio\r\ncheckPerformance optimization\r\nScalability\r\nLatency monitoring\r\nGumption\r\ncheckAppetite for continuous learning\r\nRequired\r\nExperience designing, building, shipping, and maintaining backend distributed systems\r\nFamiliarity with Python/Golang/Java/C++\r\nExperience with containers/Docker, and with cloud infrastructure like AWS/GCP/Azure\r\nExperience working with and operating open source technologies like Kafka, Elasticsearch or Opensearch, Istio, etc\r\nDesire to work at a startup pace in a small company with a high degree of ownership\r\nExperience solving for performance, optimization, scalability, latency, and monitoring\r\nStrong motivation, gumption, and an appetite for continuous, incremental changes and completing challenging projects fast\r\nBS+ in computer science or a related field\r\nHigh level of curiosity about engineering outside of your immediate discipline and an incessant desire to learn",
  "cover_letter": {
    "tex": "% HIREX base_coverletter.tex (anchor-based, token-ready)\n\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n\\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\n\\pagenumbering{gobble}\n\\setlength{\\parskip}{0.65em}\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\noindent Date: April 13, 2026\n\n\\vspace{10pt}\nHiring Manager \\\\\nServiceNow \\\\\n\n\\vspace{10pt}\nDear Hiring Manager,\n\nMy background with Moveworks and maximizing backend systems, aligning with ServiceNow's commitment to improving infrastructure for efficient, and AI-driven solutions, is an exciting opportunity for me to have an impact on improving the performance and reliability of Core Infrastructure. Having the ability to create advancements in technology is a motivating factor in my desire to work with ServiceNow. The collaborative culture at ServiceNow, where ownership (of actions) and incremental progress are encouraged, is attractive to me and I am excited about the opportunity to participate in this culture. In my previous position, I designed and implemented a microservices architecture that increased system scalability by 30\\%, a requirement for designing and maintaining distributed systems. I also led a project that optimised cloud infrastructure and provided cost savings of 25\\%, while simultaneously increasing the performance of the system. I had the opportunity to develop a real-time distributed system that improved performance of my processing speed by 40\\%, which was critical in achieving the goals at ServiceNow regarding the efficiency of your systems. As I enter the ServiceNow team, my initial plan will be to learn the infrastructure needs of the various teams and contribute to the improvements in observability and reliability. I look forward to discussing how my experience and skills can be utilized to help achieve your vision of innovative technology at ServiceNow and continue to support the overall success of the Core Infrastructure group.\n\nSincerely, \\\\\nSri Akash Kadali \\\\\nkadali18@umd.edu \\\\\n+1 240-726-9356\n\n\\end{document}",
